W: 2. Romans came across the channel,
W: All dressed up in tin and flannel,
W: Half a pint of Woad per man'll
W: Dress us more than these.
W:
W: Saxons you can waste your stitches,
W: Building beds for bugs in britches.
W: We have Woad to clothe us, which is
W: Not a nest for fleas.
W:
W: Romans, keep your armor.
W: Saxons your pyjama.
W: Hairy coats were meant for goats,
W: Gorillas, yaks, retriever dogs and llamas.
W:
W: March up Snowdon with your Woad on,
W: Never mind if we get rained or snowed on.
W: Never need a button sewed on,
W: Bottoms up to Woad!
